    {
      "id": "I_kwDODjvEJM7jXwqQ",
      "title": "Consolidate unnecessary DummyCaller contracts",
      "author": "smartcontracts",
      "number": 18784,
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/optimism",
      "body": "### Problem\n\nWe have **7 nearly-identical `DummyCaller` contracts** scattered across different deployment scripts. Each one does the same thing: stores an OPCM address in storage slot 0, then delegatecalls to it with encoded calldata. The only difference is the function signature.\n\n**Current implementations:**\n\n| File | Contract | Function |\n|------|----------|----------|\n| [`UpgradeOPChain.s.sol`](https://github.com/ethereum-optimism/optimism/blob/develop/packages/contracts-bedrock/scripts/deploy/UpgradeOPChain.s.sol#L129-L149) | `DummyCallerV1` | `upgrade(OPContractsManager.OpChainConfig[])` |\n| [`UpgradeOPChain.s.sol`](https://github.com/ethereum-optimism/optimism/blob/develop/packages/contracts-bedrock/scripts/deploy/UpgradeOPChain.s.sol#L129-L137) | `DummyCallerV2` | `upgrade(OPContractsManagerV2.UpgradeInput)` |\n| [`UpgradeSuperchainConfig.s.sol`](https://github.com/ethereum-optimism/optimism/blob/develop/packages/contracts-bedrock/scripts/deploy/UpgradeSuperchainConfig.s.sol#L86-L94) | `DummyCaller` | `upgradeSuperchainConfig(ISuperchainConfig)` |\n| [`UpgradeSuperchainConfig.s.sol`](https://github.com/ethereum-optimism/optimism/blob/develop/packages/contracts-bedrock/scripts/deploy/UpgradeSuperchainConfig.s.sol#L99-L110) | `DummyCallerV2` | `upgradeSuperchain(SuperchainUpgradeInput)` |\n| [`AddGameType.s.sol`](https://github.com/ethereum-optimism/optimism/blob/develop/packages/contracts-bedrock/scripts/deploy/AddGameType.s.sol#L106-L117) | `DummyCaller` | `addGameType(AddGameInput[])` |\n| [`InteropMigration.s.sol`](https://github.com/ethereum-optimism/optimism/blob/develop/packages/contracts-bedrock/scripts/deploy/InteropMigration.s.sol#L229-L240) | `DummyCaller` | `migrate(MigrateInput)` |\n\nAll of these follow the exact same pattern:\n```solidity\ncontract DummyCaller {\n    address internal _opcmAddr;\n\n    function someFunction(SomeType memory input) external returns (bool, bytes memory) {\n        bytes memory data = abi.encodeCall(SomeInterface.someFunction, (input));\n        (bool success, bytes memory result) = _opcmAddr.delegatecall(data);\n        return (success, result);\n    }\n}\n```\n\n### Solution\n\nReplace all of these with a single generic implementation that uses a `fallback()` function to forward any call:\n\n```solidity\n/// @title DummyCallerGeneric\n/// @notice Generic delegatecall forwarder. Reads target from storage slot 0,\n/// forwards calldata via delegatecall, reverts on failure, returns on success.\ncontract DummyCallerGeneric {\n    address internal _opcmAddr;\n\n    fallback() external {\n        address target = _opcmAddr;\n        assembly {\n            calldatacopy(0, 0, calldatasize())\n            let result := delegatecall(gas(), target, 0, calldatasize(), 0, 0)\n            returndatacopy(0, 0, returndatasize())\n            switch result\n            case 0 { revert(0, returndatasize()) }\n            default { return(0, returndatasize()) }\n        }\n    }\n}\n```\n\n### Tasks\n\n1. Move `DummyCallerGeneric` to a shared location (e.g., `scripts/libraries/DummyCaller.sol`)\n2. Update all scripts to use `DummyCaller` instead of their custom implementations\n3. Remove the redundant `DummyCallerV1`, `DummyCallerV2`, and `DummyCaller` contracts\n4. Update any Go code that references specific DummyCaller artifacts to use the generic one",
      "createdAt": "2026-01-14T19:55:45Z",
      "closedAt": "2026-01-15T17:45:07Z",
      "state": "CLOSED",
      "commentCount": 0
    },
